<title>USA: Nalco Chemical buys water treatment unit.</title>
<headline>Nalco Chemical buys water treatment unit.</headline>
<dateline>NAPERVILLE, Ill. 1996-11-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nalco Chemical Co said Monday it signed a letter of intent to acquire the outstanding shares of International Water Consultants Beheer B.V.</p>
<p>Terms of the deal were not disclosed.</p>
<p>International Water Consultants is a wholly owned subsidiary of Servo Delden B.V., a company of German-based Huls AG.</p>
<p>International Water Consultants provides water treatment services in various European countries. It is expected to post 1996 sales of about $20 million.</p>
<p>--Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787</p>
</text>
